#
# SGLang v0.5.20 + our SM121 build patches. Created 2026-09-22 to track the
# v0.5.20 line (released 2026-09-18, 713 PRs / 237 contributors). NOT BUILT
# YET: no acceptance-gate run, no GPU/serving run. Treat everything here as
# first-contact until scripts/verify_sglang_image.sh has passed on the image.
#
# THE HEADLINE: the build side is again quiet (nothing that feeds a recipe knob
# moved), but this ref is the first in the line where GB10-specific work we
# carry BY HAND landed upstream:
#   1. Qwen3.8-Flash-Next is NATIVE (#37500). python/sglang/srt/models/
#      qwen4_exp.py + qwen4_exp_mtp.py + configs/qwen4_exp.py exist in this ref,
#      including the file-backed / pinned-host PLE table for unified-memory
#      devices. The v0.5.19 capability loss (OPEN RISK F there) is REPAIRED
#      WITHOUT the 20k-line source patch: APPLY_QWEN4EXP_PR36497 stays 0 and
#      the model works anyway.
#   2. The SM121 QSA pieces our p65/p66 runtime patches backport are UPSTREAM
#      now: qwen_sparse_attn_backend._resolve_flash_attn_varlen_func() routes
#      is_sm121() to sglang.kernels.ops.attention.qwen38_qsa_sm121_varlen, and
#      the trtllm decode resolver gates on `is_sm100_supported() or is_sm120()`
#      i.e. it already EXCLUDES SM121 (that is p65 EDIT 1's veto, natively).
#      There is a real package python/sglang/kernels/kda_kernels/
#      qwen38_qsa_sm121/ with a newer kernel.py than the one p66 writes.
#      See OPEN RISK A.2; this is the thing to look at before the build, not
#      after.
#   3. The config tier became msgspec.Struct and get_global_server_args() now
#      RAISES (#38375 / #38753 / #38958). The surviving spelling is
#      get_exec().<bag>.<arg>, which is exactly what p30/p34 were re-anchored
#      to in the v0.5.19 cycle, so the runtime patches are not obviously
#      broken, but "not obviously broken" is not a replay. See OPEN RISK A.
#
# ── DELTA vs sglang-0.5.19-sm121.recipe ─────────────────────────────────────
#   1. SGLANG_VERSION 0.5.19 to 0.5.20, SGLANG_REF to v0.5.20.
#   2. SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT "-v0.5.19" to "-v0.5.20". COSMETIC this time,
#      unlike the last two bumps: the four patch BODIES are byte-identical to
#      the -v0.5.19 ones once the @@ line numbers are normalised away. #32114
#      deleted ten entries from the CMakeLists SOURCES list (cutlass_mla,
#      vertical_slash_index, awq, gptq and the five sparse-FA sources), which
#      moves the skip-sm90-target and skip-flashmla hunks by -10. The suffix is
#      moved anyway so the anchors are exact; see the NOT-A-TRIPWIRE note in
#      PATCH VERIFY.
#   3. FLASHINFER_VERSION UNCHANGED at 0.6.18.post1. v0.5.20 still pins
#      flashinfer_python[cu13]==0.6.18, so the pin policy (newest stable inside
#      the ref's pinned version) lands on the same wheel as last cycle. Do NOT
#      reach for 0.7.0; it is outside the ref's pin.
#   4. BASE_IMAGE / TRANSFORMERS / KERNELS / CUTLASS_DSL / HF_HUB / TOKENIZERS /
#      AUDIO / ACCELERATE / SGL_KERNEL_DIR / TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT: ALL
#      UNCHANGED. v0.5.20 still pins torch==2.13.0, transformers==5.12.1,
#      kernels>=0.14.1,<0.15, nvidia-cutlass-dsl[cu13]==4.6.2, tokenizers==0.22.2.
#   5. APPLY_QWEN4EXP_PR36497 stays 0, but for the OPPOSITE reason than on
#      v0.5.19: there it was 0 because the branch diff no longer applied and the
#      model was therefore unavailable; here it is 0 because the model is NATIVE
#      (#37500). Turning it on would abort the in-container dry-run.
#      roles/k8s_dgx/model_profiles/radixark-qwen3.8-flash-next-nvfp4.yml still
#      PINS 0.5.18-sm121; moving it to this tag is a deliberate, separate change
#      and depends on OPEN RISK A.2 (TP4).
#   6. Every other APPLY_* flag keeps its v0.5.19 value; the reasons are
#      re-verified against this ref in PATCH VERIFY below, not carried over.
#   7. Upstream dependency churn that rides along with the ref (informational,
#      none of it a knob here): sglang-kernel 0.4.6.post1 -> 0.4.7 (#39346),
#      sgl-deep-gemm 0.1.7 -> 0.2.0 (#39371), smg-grpc-servicer floor >=0.5.0 ->
#      >=0.9.0, NEW dependency nvshmem4py-cu13 (unpinned), sgl-eval==0.1.0 added
#      to the [test] extra only. sgl-deep-ep stays 0.1.2, tilelang 0.1.12,
#      compressed-tensors 0.18.0, quack-kernels 0.6.4, cuda-tile 1.6.0rc5 and
#      apache-tvm-ffi 0.1.11 unchanged. aarch64 wheels verified on PyPI
#      2026-09-22 for all three moved/new packages: sglang_kernel-0.4.7-cp310-
#      abi3-manylinux2014_aarch64, sgl_deep_gemm-0.2.0-py3-none-
#      manylinux2014_aarch64, nvshmem4py_cu13-0.3.1-cp312-manylinux2014_aarch64.
#
# ── PATCH VERIFY (2026-09-22, host-side, against raw v0.5.20 source) ─────────
#   OK sgl-kernel-arch-prune-v0.5.20.patch        regenerated, content identical
#   OK sgl-kernel-disable-fa3-v0.5.20.patch       regenerated, content identical
#   OK sgl-kernel-skip-sm90-target-v0.5.20.patch  regenerated, content identical
#   OK sgl-kernel-skip-flashmla-v0.5.20.patch     regenerated, content identical
#      Produced the same way as the -v0.5.19 set: apply in build order, re-diff
#      each step against the previous one, so all four land with ZERO fuzz and
#      ZERO offset. Re-applying the whole set to pristine v0.5.20 reproduces the
#      sequential reference tree byte for byte and leaves the eight "dgxarley
#      ..." markers in place (arch-prune x2, disable-fa3 x1, skip-sm90-target
#      x4, skip-flashmla x1).
#      NOT A TRIPWIRE THIS TIME: unlike the v0.5.18 -> v0.5.19 step, the
#      -v0.5.19 files do NOT fail on v0.5.20 (all four apply, two at offset -10)
#      and the -v0.5.20 files do not fail on v0.5.19 (offset +18 on
#      skip-sm90-target). A recipe that forgets to move the suffix therefore
#      builds a CORRECT tree instead of aborting loudly. Do not read the
#      previous cycles' "the cross-check protects us" note as still true here.
#   OK sglang-dsv4-mtp-marlin-v0.5.14.patch       applies (offset 246); still
#      NEEDED: HybridFp8NvFp4Config.get_quant_method in v0.5.20 still goes
#      straight to Mxfp4FlashinferTrtllmMoEMethod with no marlin branch
#      (modelopt_quant.py:1683-1699).
#   OK sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch  applies (offset 11);
#      path python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/tilelang_kernel.py unchanged.
#   NO sglang-qwen4exp-pr36497.patch              NATIVE in this ref, GATED OFF.
#      See DELTA 5 / the headline.
#   NO sglang-nemotron35-spec-pr36186.patch       MERGED since v0.5.19, GATED OFF.
#   NO sgl-kernel-sm121.patch                     target still gone, GATED OFF.
#      python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/moe/nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh does not exist
#      in v0.5.20 either (verified 2026-09-22), so NVFP4 MoE keeps running
#      through FlashInfer-CUTLASS. MoeRunnerBackend.CUTLASS still exists as an
#      enum member; the NVFP4 kernel behind it does not.
#   -- Dockerfile chain NOT re-verified for this ref yet. scitrera
#      cuda-containers origin/main is UNCHANGED at 2a3b1b7 (checked 2026-09-22),
#      the same commit the v0.5.19 chain was clean against, and the three
#      dockerfile patches target the Dockerfile rather than sglang; the build
#      dry-runs them anyway.
#
# ── OPEN RISKS, validate before this recipe is promoted ──────────────────────
#   A. RUNTIME patches (roles/k8s_dgx/files/sglang_patches/): NOT REPLAYED
#      against this ref. This is the gate on promoting the recipe, same as it
#      was for v0.5.19. Re-run the spark5 harness (/root/patchreplay-0519,
#      `SRC=dist-src TAG=0520 ./replay2.sh`) with v0.5.19 as the control. Two
#      things are known to need attention BEFORE that replay rather than after:
#      A.1 CONFIG TIER. #38375 removed seventeen deprecated CLI flags and made
#          get_global_server_args() raise; #38753 / #38958 turned ServerArgs and
#          the rest of the config tier into msgspec.Struct, so dataclasses.asdict
#          and dataclass introspection on it no longer work. The surviving read
#          is get_exec().<bag>.<arg>, which p30 and p34 already carry as their
#          newest replace_any spelling, so the expectation is drift in the
#          patches that still reach for a ServerArgs OBJECT (p59's
#          model_config_of(server_args) body header is the first to check), not
#          a wholesale rewrite. The retired name appears in our tree only in
#          historical replace_any spellings (p34) and in _patchlib's docstring.
#      A.2 p65 AND p66 ARE PROBABLY REDUNDANT HERE, AND p66 IS PROBABLY STILL
#          NEEDED AT TP4. Both are backports of SM121 QSA work that this ref
#          contains natively:
#            * p65 EDIT 1 (trtllm veto on SM121): native. The decode resolver
#              in qwen_sparse_attn_backend.py returns None unless
#              is_sm100_supported() or is_sm120(), so SM121 never reaches the
#              trtllm kernel that produced the silent "!"-runs.
#            * p65 EDIT 2 (route SM121 off the flash_attn cute fallback) and
#              p66 (write the kernel package + registry entry + routing):
#              native. _resolve_flash_attn_varlen_func() early-returns
#              qwen38_qsa_sm121_varlen on is_sm121(), and the package
#              python/sglang/kernels/kda_kernels/qwen38_qsa_sm121/ ships with a
#              NEWER kernel.py than the one p66 pins (upstream sha256
#              a648b2c7..., p66 pins a0fd7258...).
#            * WHAT IS STILL OURS: the shape contract. Upstream's wrapper
#              accepts BF16 / D=256 / 12:1 GQA as 24Q+2KV (TP1) or 12Q+1KV
#              (TP2) and RAISES "unsupported SM121 QSA call" otherwise. TP4
#              (6Q + 1KV) is exactly what p66 widened by hand, and exactly how
#              this cluster runs the model. So p66 most likely has to be
#              reshaped from "write the whole package" into "widen the native
#              can_use_qwen38_qsa_sm121 check", and p65 retired. Do NOT just
#              let the two patches run against this ref and hope the
#              already-applied guards catch it.
#   B. INHERITED from v0.5.16, still open: moe_runner_backend cutlass / triton
#      for NVFP4 is gone (#30448), so nvidia/Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-NVFP4 (cutlass)
#      and Minimax-M2.5 @ PP=4 (triton) still need re-testing or re-pinning, and
#      compressed-tensors NVFP4 MoE with apply_router_weight_on_input=True still
#      asserts instead of running. See TURBOQUANT.md.
#   C. NEW in v0.5.20, from the release's own "Breaking Changes":
#      * SM120 FP8 LINEAR LAYERS WITH PER-CHANNEL WEIGHT SCALES now take the
#        per-tensor route (cudnn/nvjet) instead of channelwise CUTLASS (#38006).
#        This is the one breaking change that lands squarely on our hardware
#        class; re-measure the FP8 profiles rather than carrying verdicts. The
#        same PR family raises the decode CUDA-graph cap 24 -> 48 (160 at
#        TP >= 4) and chunked prefill 2K -> 4K on 32 GB GPUs (#37898).
#      * cutlass_mla attention backend, the non-Marlin gptq choice, the AWQ AOT
#        dequantize kernel and Dual Chunk Flash Attention are DELETED (#32114).
#        GPTQ keeps working through gptq_marlin; auto-round and moe_wna16 lose
#        their non-Marlin GPU fallback. p20 (moe_wna16 qzeros EP) is the patch
#        to look at if any moe_wna16 profile is still in use.
#      * An undersized SWA pool now fails at startup with ValueError instead of
#        hanging at warmup (#37610).
#      * /v1/responses no longer stores results unless --enable-response-store
#        is passed; retrieval, previous_response_id chaining and background
#        requests return 400 without it (#39122). Nothing here uses them today,
#        but LiteLLM/Hermes talk to /v1/chat/completions, not /v1/responses,
#        confirm that before assuming it is inert.
#      * --dcp-comm-backend now resolves per platform (#37767 / #39165);
#        --sampling-mask-max-tokens replaces the old env var (#36631); prefill
#        CP v1 and the SGLANG_ENABLE_CP_V2 gate are removed (#36228). None of
#        these are set on our profiles.
#      * gRPC GetIsReady replaced by the WatchEngineState stream (#39915). We
#        serve HTTP, not gRPC.
#      Carried over from v0.5.19 and still true: the unified radix tree is the
#      default cache for every model (#35081), DeepSeek-V4 FP4 expert
#      checkpoints default to the FlashInfer MXFP4 MoE runner when
#      --moe-runner-backend is auto (#35919, our profiles pin the backend
#      explicitly), and requests are capped at 32 stop strings / 32 stop regexes
#      (#37029).
#   D. TORCH: no gap. v0.5.20 still pins torch==2.13.0 (torchaudio 2.11.0), which
#      is exactly what BASE_IMAGE ships. No new base build for this recipe.
#   E. INHERITED dependency shapes the missing_deps step will try to install:
#      cuda-tile==1.6.0rc5 still has no PyPI wheel for that version (wheel-stub
#      sdist redirecting to pypi.nvidia.com; fix is --extra-index-url
#      https://pypi.nvidia.com, not unpinning). NEW this cycle: nvshmem4py-cu13
#      is unpinned upstream and resolves to 0.3.1 (aarch64 cp312 wheel exists),
#      and sgl-deep-gemm moved to a new major 0.2.0. missing_deps.py only checks
#      PRESENCE, not version, so a package already installed from the previous
#      layer stays at its old version; check sgl-deep-gemm on the built image.
#   F. SM12x WORK IN v0.5.20 WE HAVE NOT EXERCISED, check for redundancy BEFORE
#      re-porting runtime anchors (same lesson as v0.5.16's
#      fp8_paged_mqa_logits_torch_sm120 absorption and as A.2 above):
#      #29927 puts the DeepSeek-V4 sparse-MLA indexer on DeepGEMM's paged-MQA
#      kernel on SM120 and enables the DeepGEMM FP4 MoE backend there, replacing
#      exactly the torch fallback that p30 installs by hand. It is opt-in
#      behind env flags, and it is the single most likely thing to make p30/p34/
#      p35 unnecessary (or wrong). See reference_glm52_dsa_indexer_deepgemm_sm121
#      and reference_dsv4_sm121_dsa_kernels before touching those three.
#      Also unexercised: #30805 (TRT-LLM DSv4 attention, SM100/103 only),
#      #31470 (--moe-runner-backend flashinfer_megamoe) and the new
#      GLM-5.3-Flash / Hy4-Preview / K2-Horizon cookbook entries.
#   G. INHERITED: NVFP4 ATTENTION on SM121 (flashinfer #3897) is still only
#      KERNEL-level verified (2026-07-28 on spark5), never validated end to end
#      through SGLang with a real uniform-NVFP4 model. flashinfer does NOT move
#      this cycle (0.6.18.post1 on both refs), so the v0.5.19 verdicts are at
#      least not invalidated by a driver bump, but they were never taken on a
#      built 0.5.19 image either. Judge output quality by pattern-grep plus
#      token distribution plus tail, not by finish_reason.
#
# ── DEPLOY NOTE: SGLANG_CACHE_DIR (#32434, since v0.5.18) ───────────────────
# Triton, FlashInfer, Inductor, DeepGEMM and the CUDA driver cache all live
# under SGLANG_CACHE_DIR, so the FIRST launch on this image recompiles once.
# Setting any of TRITON_CACHE_DIR / FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE /
# SGLANG_DG_CACHE_DIR / TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR / CUDA_CACHE_PATH keeps that one
# where it is. We already set FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE explicitly in
# roles/k8s_dgx/tasks/sglang_instance.yml, so the expensive flashinfer JIT cache
# is NOT affected; the DeepGEMM cache is, and is the other expensive one.
#
# Prerequisite: xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.13.0-v1-cu132 present on the
# build host (scripts/build_pytorch_base_image.sh, see ensure_base_image_present
# in build_sm121_image.sh). UNCHANGED from v0.5.18/v0.5.19; it is already there
# if either of those images was built.
#
DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
TARGET=runtime

# UNCHANGED from the v0.5.19 recipe: v0.5.20 still pins torch==2.13.0
# (torchaudio 2.11.0), so the 2.13.0-v1-cu132 base built 2026-08-28 still
# matches upstream exactly. Do NOT rebuild the base for this recipe.
BASE_IMAGE=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.13.0-v1-cu132

# flashinfer 0.6.18.post1 - UNCHANGED from the v0.5.19 recipe. v0.5.20 still
# pins flashinfer_python[cu13]==0.6.18 (python/pyproject.toml:42, "keep it
# aligned with jit-cache version in Dockerfile"), so "newest stable inside the
# ref's pin" resolves to the same wheel as last cycle. 0.7.0 exists on PyPI and
# is OUTSIDE the pin; do not reach for it to work around a 0.5.20 problem.
# The v0.5.19 rationale still applies underneath: .post1 is 0.6.18 plus exactly
# one additive cherry-pick (#4931) and a version bump, and the 0.6.18 content
# that matters here is MXFP4 MoE coverage extended to DGX Spark plus the older
# #3932 (b12x FP4 quantization numerics fix, the reason W4A4 output quality has
# to be re-measured rather than carried over), #3897 / #3838 / #3960 / #3922.
# One dependency note from this ref: #37206 dropped SGLang's in-tree MNNVL CuTe
# DSL port in favour of FlashInfer 0.6.18's, so the pin is now load-bearing for
# that path too.
#
# Wheels re-verified 2026-09-22 on https://flashinfer.ai/whl, including the one
# that matters for arm64:
#   flashinfer-jit-cache 0.6.18.post1+cu130 manylinux_2_28_aarch64
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.18
FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.18.post1

# transformers 5.12.1 - exactly v0.5.20's pyproject pin (==5.12.1, unchanged
# since v0.5.15). Do NOT bump past the SGLang ref (no perf benefit, transformers
# is not in the inference hot path).
TRANSFORMERS_VERSION=5.12.1

# kernels 0.14.1 - exactly v0.5.20's constraint (kernels>=0.14.1,<0.15,
# unchanged). PERF-NEUTRAL on SM121: the only hub-loaded kernel
# (sgl-flash-attn3) is hard-disabled on GB10 and has no sm_121/ARM64 builds.
KERNELS_VERSION=0.14.1

# nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.6.2 - UNCHANGED, still exactly v0.5.20's pyproject pin
# (nvidia-cutlass-dsl[cu13]==4.6.2). The explicit pin stays mandatory because
# NVIDIA has shipped different wheel CONTENT under the same version number
# before (the 4.5.2 mlir_global_dtors 'data' ICE, see
# reference_cutlass_dsl_wheel_swap).
# Re-verify on the built image with the rmsnorm smoke test from the v0.5.18
# recipe (and confirm the DSL path is actually TAKEN: norm/__init__.py falls
# back to CUDA JIT SILENTLY when the DSL cannot target the arch).
# Fallback: 4.6.1, then 4.6.0.
CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.6.2

# Audio multimodal deps - see the 0.5.15.post1 recipe. SGLang pulls numba itself;
# librosa is still needed (soundfile/audioread).
AUDIO_DEPS="librosa"

# accelerate - baked into the image (ModelOptModelLoader imports it).
ACCELERATE_DEPS="accelerate"

# huggingface_hub FLOOR (not an exact pin), unchanged. Guards against the xet
# gated-repo download bug (hub PR #4394 forwarded the REDACTED xetHash for GATED
# repos to hf_xet -> "Unable to parse string as hex hash value"); fixed by hub
# PR #4595 in v1.26.0. See FIXED_UPSTREAM_HF_XET_BUG.md. Installed as the LAST
# pip action of the builder stage so nothing can downgrade it afterwards.
HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION=1.26.0

# tokenizers 0.22.2 - exactly v0.5.20's pyproject pin, UNCHANGED from v0.5.19.
# The knob is still needed for the same reason it was introduced: missing_deps.py
# checks presence and not version, and the late transformers step installs with
# --pre, so pip may otherwise resolve 0.23.0rc0 inside transformers' own
# tokenizers>=0.22.0,<=0.23.0 range (which is what the first 0.5.19-sm121 image
# shipped). Enforced by scripts/patches/dockerfile-tokenizers-pin.patch as the
# last pip action of the builder stage.
TOKENIZERS_VERSION=0.22.2

SGLANG_VERSION=0.5.20
SGLANG_REF="v0.5.20"

# main-ahead sgl-kernel patch variant. Kept at 1 for provenance (the -v0.5.20
# files carry the mainahead content, the mscclpp link refactor is still in the
# tree), but SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT takes precedence in apply_patches(), so
# the -mainahead siblings themselves are not used on this ref.
SGL_KERNEL_MAINAHEAD=1

# Suffix of the four CMakeLists source patches to install under the canonical
# names. "-v0.5.20" = the -v0.5.19 edits re-anchored against v0.5.20; the patch
# BODIES are byte-identical, only the hunk line numbers move (#32114 shortened
# the SOURCES list by ten lines above the skip-sm90-target / skip-flashmla
# regions). All four regenerated with zero fuzz and zero offset. Note that the
# -v0.5.19 set does NOT fail loudly on this ref, so the suffix is discipline,
# not a tripwire.
SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.20"

# Where the sgl-kernel tree lives inside the sglang checkout (moved there by RFC
# #29630 in v0.5.17), passed to the Dockerfile as ARG SGL_KERNEL_DIR (default
# "sgl-kernel", so older recipes are byte-identical). UNCHANGED in v0.5.20 (the
# package version moved 0.4.6.post1 -> 0.4.7, the path did not); MUST match the
# path in the patch variant above.
SGL_KERNEL_DIR=python/sglang/kernels/aot

# ── CORE SM121 JIT-header patch: TARGET STILL GONE (PR #30448) -> OFF ────────
# python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/moe/nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh has not returned in
# v0.5.20 (verified 2026-09-22) and cutlass_moe_fp4() is still absent; NVFP4 MoE
# runs through FlashInfer-CUTLASS on SM100/SM120/SM121, the backend our model
# profiles pin anyway (moe_runner_backend: flashinfer_cutlass). At 1 the
# in-container dry-run would abort the build. Consequence: see OPEN RISK B.
APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 FlashMLA kernel: DROPPED (native since v0.5.13) ──────────────
FLASH_MLA_REPO=
FLASH_MLA_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_REPO=
DSV4_KERNEL_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_ARCH=

# ── DeepSeek-V4 NVFP4 MoE: NATIVE since v0.5.14 (PR #25820) -> OFF ──────────
APPLY_DSV4_NVFP4_PR25820=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 EAGLE-MTP marlin branch + TileLang indexer compat -> ON ──────
# Unchanged rationale: HybridFp8NvFp4Config.get_quant_method still has no marlin
# branch for the MTP/nextn draft-MoE layers in v0.5.20 (it goes straight to
# Mxfp4FlashinferTrtllmMoEMethod, verified 2026-09-22), and the TileLang uint8
# arg check still bites. Both source patches dry-run-verified against v0.5.20
# on 2026-09-22 (marlin: offset 246; tilelang: offset 11).
APPLY_DSV4_MTP_MARLIN_TILELANG=1

# Variant of the tilelang compat patch. "-v0.5.16" selects
# sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch: the path introduced by RFC
# #29630 (python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/) and only the uint8-view hunk,
# because upstream adopted the 2D alloc_shared half. That file name is a
# GENERATION label, not a ref restriction; the path and the hunk are unchanged
# in v0.5.20, verified applying at offset 11.
TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.16"

# ── Qwen3.6 ModelOpt mixed NVFP4: MERGED (PR #27906) -> OFF ─────────────────
# The OPEN dispatch fix #28099 is a RUNTIME patch in sglang_launch.sh and is
# unaffected by this flag (p21/p22); re-check Qwen3.6 live.
APPLY_QWEN36_MIXED_NVFP4_PR27906=0

# ── Qwen4-Exp / Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: NATIVE since this ref (PR #37500) -> OFF ─
# The reason flipped between v0.5.19 and here. On v0.5.19 this was 0 because the
# v0.5.18-based branch diff no longer applied, which cost us the model. On
# v0.5.20 it is 0 because upstream MERGED it: python/sglang/srt/models/
# qwen4_exp.py + qwen4_exp_mtp.py + configs/qwen4_exp.py exist (verified
# 2026-09-22), including the pinned-host / file-backed PLE embedding for
# unified-memory devices that the GB10 branch commits carried. Applying the
# 20k-line source patch on top would abort the in-container dry-run.
# The profile roles/k8s_dgx/model_profiles/radixark-qwen3.8-flash-next-nvfp4.yml
# still PINS 0.5.18-sm121; repointing it here is a separate change gated on
# OPEN RISK A.2 (the native SM121 QSA kernel does not accept TP4).
APPLY_QWEN4EXP_PR36497=0

# -- Nemotron 3.5 Lightning speculative decoding: NATIVE since v0.5.19 -> OFF -
# v0.5.19 already contained 41e7612dee (PR #36186 plus its two DFlash2
# prerequisites #35371 and #35496), and v0.5.20 is a descendant of it, so the
# MTP / DFlash / DSpark drafts for
# nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-NVFP4 are native here too.
# Re-applying merged code fails the in-container dry-run and aborts the build.
APPLY_NEMOTRON35_SPEC_PR36186=0

IMAGE_TAG=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-sglang:0.5.20-sm121
